  "title": "A plain crossing inside braces",
  "subject": "Whether plain Pfaffian braces can simulate a crossing",
  "conclusion": "Ladders of plain cube junctions with rungs act by (NW)^k with characteristic polynomial (x^2 - 19x - 1)(x^2 + 7x + 13), whose roots, a unit of Q(sqrt 365) and the Eisenstein primes above 13, satisfy the lattice condition, so interpolation over odd k yields an exact crossing. K3,3 is counted from plain Pfaffian braces of 20 to 104 vertices.",
